P4. Legacy calls.

At the SIGSYS stop of a call Android's policy traps, fork becomes
clone(SIGCHLD, 0), with the argument registers restored in the parent at its
sysexit and in the child at its first stop; mknod, creat, pause, alarm,
epoll_create, inotify_init, signalfd and eventfd become the calls the policy
allows; dup2(a, a) is answered from /proc/<pid>/fd/<a>; setuid, setgid,
setreuid and setregid succeed only when they change no id; setfsuid and
setfsgid return the current id; and the other calls bionic's blocklist names
return EPERM. trapped-calls.txt lists every trapped call and how it is
answered. alloc_mem reserves the red zone at every allocation.

